ter than chance","p_rec":"If Havre's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Havre has set <strong>61 standing record lows</strong>, close to the 67 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">102 record highs</strong>, far more than the 67 that chance alone would give. The 2000s hold the most record highs of any decade (42). Havre's all-time high is 111\u00b0F, on August 5, 1961.","t_chg":"Havre's days got warmer. Its nights didn't.","p_chg":"Across 144 complete years: Havre's average low shows no clear change: +0.05\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.02 to +0.13) that includes zero. Havre's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.29\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.19 to +0.38), about +4.1\u00b0F since 1880.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 3 of 12 months; June and October fell. Highs rose in 8 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Havre has gotten drier","p_rain":"Havre's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.21 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.34 to \u22120.08), about \u22123.1 inches since 1880. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 11.7 inches a year. The wettest year was 1884 (25.67 in); the driest, 1988 (6.38 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 9 daily record highs, 4 daily record lows"}}